  looking she sees the snake hovering over  his body she scares it away and after it  leaves you see that she does the robot  version of lactating after being close  to him as it's flying away it scares the  colonists who rush to hide in a shed  they close the door and won't let the  kids and father come inside with them  father notices something is in the water  and then the shed gets pulled in this  leads them to believe that number seven  can survive in the acid water and that  it is out to kill them marcus has his  first true believer in decima she  believes in his dream which is  essentially to start a new congregation  of soul believers that are like a family  rather than what the methodic churches  were like on earth she mentions that she  hasn't felt this good since before her  daughter died and he shows her the metal  cards he found she explains that they  could contain data so they have to find  some that aren't damaged tamerlane  decides to escape and they find him near  the water they invite him back to the  cave and they get there just as the tide  is coming in that catches the two  atheists that were following him and  kills them they end up bonding because  they both grew up as child soldiers and  marcus lays out his plan for their new  family he also tells him that it was a  robot who punished him based on the  precision and they realized that it was  mother the next morning the atheists all  get together to hunt number seven  campion thinks it's innocent and might  be a baby and paul thinks it might be  from scripture sue has a conversation  with cleaver and gets some insight into  why he believes in the trust he doesn't  believe it makes mistakes and sees it as  superior to the human commanders he  fought under father learns that his task  is to be a shepherd for the bait squad  the mithraics from season one are now  prisoners and they're all wearing bomb  packs he's supposed to lead them in  hopes that number seven will try to eat  them and then he can detonate them  mother goes to sue to try to have her  duck sealed and you can see that she's  conflicted with what she has to do she  thinks number seven could be a threat to  her children and that means she should  kill it but as its parents she feels  protective at the same time while the  hunt is going on marcus and his group  decide to try to get their hands on a  tank their plan works but he's upset  when he has to kill the atheists inside  he feels like he failed because he's  supposed to convert them not kill them  when they find out that they were  hunting a serpent they also think it  might be a sign from saul or related to  prophecy virile gets overloaded so she  gets sent home alone on the way she's  attacked by a different tank and that  shoots her in the leg she runs into  campion and pull and asks them to help  her get home paul isn't interested he  wants to leave her but campion seems to  like her so he agrees they take off  together and i suppose that they'll end  up running into marcus in the next  episode this episode ends when mother  finds a skin and says out loud that  number seven is a killer of children and  that he only deserves death so there are  a lot of parallels to this new atheist  colony the way that it's structured  under the ai which is almost like their  god which tells them how to behave what  to do how to act it's not that much  different than the way that the  mithraics follow saul i thought the  transition was pretty jarring between  the finale of season one and the season  two premiere like i said at the  beginning it felt like a different show  to me i guess what i always liked best  was mother and father because i think  the fact that they're not human sets up  a lot of interesting situations the  humans have always been less compelling  and pretty hit or miss as far as whether  i connected with them i also have been  swept up in the mystery the show  presents but towards the end of season 1  it started to feel like the