 a.i that is guiding their group  which is called the collective decima is  a methodic engineer who was working on  the ark before the atheists stole it and  she has an android with her name virile  who will learn is a replacement for her  daughter that died there's also an  atheist named cleaver who in contrast to  tamerlane seems absolutely loyal to the  ai even going as far as saying he'd be  fine with taking orders from it for the  rest of his life you're introduced to  the trust after mother wakes up to find  a tech rooting around inside her abdomen  she demands to be taken to him after she  takes control of the situation and  here's the ai call to her because it was  also created by campion sturgis it calls  her sister and they seem to get along  swimmingly it notices she has some  encrypted files hidden inside of her  memory and she explains that she feels  things impulses and one of those is to  conceal the parts of herself that  displease her she asked about number  seven the android serpent hybrid she  gave birth to and the trust thinks that  since the lander was destroyed anything  inside would have been two though as  viewers we know this isn't the case  mother learns that all of the children  have been rescued and that thanks to her  all that remains of the mithraic threat  is a lone terrorist he's referring to  marcus who starts out the season 3 000  miles away where he shoots down a ship  and then tries to use that to attack the  ark the trust takes control of the ship  before he can do that and then he shoots  the controls which causes him to crash  into the ocean which is unfortunate  since it's actually filled with acid  he's able to escape and while he's  wandering around he finds some of those  metal cards with the symbols on them  that we saw a couple of times in season  one remember mother had her vision of  the ancient ceremony when she scanned  one of those marcus eventually finds a  cave and is surprised to find that there  is a temple inside dedicated to soul  this all feeds into a sense that he's  being guided by the deity later when  he's out gathering food he sees decima  and varial trying to escape from the  collective they had those bomb packs  strapped to them and the other prisoner  who told them that he knew how to remove  them tried to take his off it detonated  luckily marcus knows that an android  shoulder pin looks the same as a pack  key so he digs out varials and uses it  to free them because of his  well-documented hatred for them he did  want to leave the android behind but  decimal was able to convince him to free  them both he brings them back to his  cave and explains that soul wants him to  fill the temple with believers  mother and father are reunited with the  children paul was kept a little longer  because they quarantined him after they  found out he was hearing voices the kids  are split on being part of this atheist  colony and the members don't really want  them there either they tend to blame the  two mythic made androids and their  adopted mythic children for destroying  earth during the war the trust explains  that mother has been reprogrammed to  fight for them but the colonists have  good reasons to be wary of necromancers  even though lamia doesn't have her eyes  to weaponize her beyond that this is a  big upgrade from their old settlement  the weather is good food is plentiful  they have a nice dwelling to stay in and  as father says this side of the planet  is less intent on trying to kill their  children there's still some weirdness  between mother and father remember he  started to have human-like feelings that  resembled jealousy when he found out she  got pregnant but he's decided to  postpone the erasing of his memories of  their time together paul doesn't want  sue around so she decides to get  reassigned to a different group when  mother questions her on why she decided  to tell him about killing his real  parents she explains that she didn't  that a voice inside his head told him  the truth mother mentions what happened  to her inside the sim vaguely and  wonders if this is a transmission  capable of affecting humans and androids  this set sue on a path to try to figure  out where the voice is coming from you  learn that the trust plans out  everything for the colonists and they  each get daily tasks and you also see  that there are punishments the kids and  father all get the task of gathering  food while mother is assigned to the  nursery while they're gathering father  and vita find a cave where inside they  find pieces of an ancient android paul  finds a dodecahedron under a tree and  campion finds an egg the artifact has  the tree of life symbol so the prophecy  of the orphan boy is brought up talk of  the pentagonal prophecy in the tree of  life leads to a discussion over saul  which they both agree exists at least as  far as the voice that everyone is  hearing but campion thinks that it's  evil because it would be against the  rules to keep what they found they make  a pact to keep each other's secrets  later when they're looking at them at  home paul says he thinks there might be  a map or seeds inside to grow the tree  he's thinking that maybe it hasn't been  planted yet and while they're talking  someone comes up and burns the soul  symbol outside of their dwelling as a  threat and the first episode ends there  episode 2 opens with marcus sitting by  the water and we see decima come up to  sit by him she prays and then she says  that she can feel soul's light burning  inside of him that he's the only human  being that she's ever wanted to touch  this is all likely because he has  mother's necromancer eyes inside of him  but he never tells anybody about what's  going on after she hears what happens  sue brings the kids a gun for protection  after they leave she tells mother that  she found out that there is a signal but  that it can't penetrate the emf that  covers the tropical zone they don't know  where the transmission is coming from  but this leads her to believe that they  may be safest right where they're at  when mother goes to the nursery she  learns that the trust has a different  assignment for her she has to be the  punisher for the day she has to wear  this suit that they found on the ark to  conceal her identity and then after she  puts on the disguise she has to go into  a room and beat tamerlane this  traumatizes her and when she goes to  tell father she sees that he's collected  a lot of pieces of this ancient android  and he says that they date back nearly a  million years when he exposed them to  light berry started to grow on them  which set up what was probably my  favorite father line of the episodes  when he said that he made some  fascinating discoveries regarding  synthetic botanicals mother explains  that she had to punish the person that  set the fire and father is just  delighted that there's justice in this  place even for them he tells her that  his caregiving protocols are satisfied  like never before and they agree that  they're in sync in that regard mother  brings up that she wants champion to be  the one to take the baton when the trust  is ready to hand over control father is  concerned that this desire might be  related to what happened with number  seven  while they're having dinner tempest  mentions that she's thinking of having  her child raised with the others in the  collective their meal is interrupted by  tamerlane who as part of his punishment  has to come to personally express  remorse about the fire his injuries are  serious so when champion sees them he  decides that he better come clean with  mother and father about the things  they'd been hiding in their room he  knows this is going to make paul upset  so mother agrees to say that she found  it on her own and she tells him to  return the egg to its nest while he's  doing that number 7 shows up and  approaches him he ends up falling and  gets knocked out so when mother comes  looking she sees the snake hovering over  his body she scares it away and after it  leaves you see that she does the robot  version of lactating after being close  to him as it's flying away it scares the  colonists who rush to hide in a shed  they close the door and won't let the  kids and father come inside with them  father notices something is in the water  and then the shed gets pulled in this  leads them to believe that number seven  can survive in the acid water and that  it is out to kill them marcus has his  first true believer in decima she  believes in his dream which is  essentially to start a new congregation  of soul believers that are like a family  rather than what the methodic churches  were like on earth she mentions that she  hasn't felt this good since before her  daughter died and he shows her the metal  cards he found she explains that they  could contain data so they have to find  some that aren't damaged tamerlane  decides to escape and they find him near  the water they invite him back to the  cave and they get there just as the tide  is coming in that catches the two  atheists that were following him and  kills them they end up bonding because  they both grew up as child soldiers and  marcus lays out his plan for their new  family he also tells him that it was a  robot who punished him based on the  precision and they realized that it was  mother the next morning the atheists all  get together to hunt number seven  campion thinks it's innocent and might  be a baby and paul thinks it might be  from scripture sue has a conversation  with cleaver and gets some insight into  why he believes in the trust he doesn't  believe it makes mistakes and sees it as  superior to the human commanders he  fought under father learns that his task  is to be a shepherd for the bait squad  the mithraics from season one are now  prisoners and they're all wearing bomb  packs he's supposed to lead them in  hopes that number seven will try to eat  them and then he can detonate them  mother goes to sue to try to have her  duck sealed and you can see that she's  conflicted with what she has to do she  thinks number seven could be a threat to  her children and that means she should  kill it but as its parents she feels  protective at the same time while the  hunt is going on marcus and his group  decide to try to get their hands on a  tank their plan works but he's upset  when he has to kill the atheists inside  he feels like he failed because he's  supposed to convert them not kill them  when they find out that they were  hunting a serpent they also think it  might be a sign from saul or related to  prophecy virile gets overloaded so she  gets sent home alone on the way she's  attacked by a different tank and that  shoots her in the leg she runs into  campion and pull and asks them to help  her get home paul isn't interested he  wants to leave her but campion seems to  like her so he agrees they take off  together and i suppose that they'll end  up running into marcus in the next  episode this episode ends when mother  finds a skin and says out loud that  number seven is a killer of children and  that he only deserves death so there are  a lot of parallels to this new atheist  colony the way that it's structured  under the ai which is almost like their  god which tells them how to behave what  to do how to act it's not that much  different than the way that the  mithraics follow saul i thought the  transition was pretty jarring between  the finale of season one and the season  two premiere like i said at the  beginning it felt like a different show  to me i guess what i always liked best  was mother and father because i think  the fact that they're not human sets up  a lot of interesting situations the  humans have always been less compelling  and pretty hit or miss as far as whether  i connected with them i also have been  swept up in the mystery the show  presents but towards the end of season 1  it started to feel like they were  continuing to pile a bunch of new ones  on without delivering any meaningful  answers so when they jump into a brand  new location with lots of new human  characters that aren't really that  fleshed out it does feel like it's  getting away from the parts of it that i  enjoyed the most that said there's a lot  of sci-fi potential with the trust and  what's going on in the collective and as  far as the mysteries i do feel like they  have a grand idea planned out they're  working towards something going  somewhere so let's get down into some of  those pits and discover more artifacts  and creatures that are evolving  backwards or whatever's going on there i  like this show when it gets weird and  takes some chances and here in these  episodes it had to do a lot of work with  this shift between episodes 10 and 11.  so i did like that there are a lot of  artifacts laying around that there was  some movement as far as sue knowing that  there's a transmission going out and  then little details like father's  android being a million years old so i'm  still curious to see where it's all  going and even though these weren't my  favorite episodes of the show i do  realize that they had a lot of setting  up to do because of the way that they  structured the story mother being  conflicted makes sense and she is  keeping that all to herself father  absolutely kills me he's by far my  favorite character and i'm really  looking forward to see what happens when  he brings this ancient android back to  life marcus appears to have some powers  or at least something going on after  ingesting the necromancer eyes and  everyone is looking at the prophecies  and applying them however they see fit  and i think that's a good place to leave  things let me know in the comments what  you thought about these first two  episodes what are the biggest questions  you have at this point in the story and  what are you hoping to see in the next  episode please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon


